    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223">

                <pb facs="0449" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2394</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-10T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 10, 1916, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 11, 8.15 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>90. Department’s telegram 48,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d223-f1"/> February 7. Am
                    informed that no passengers on boats sunk. Warning shot given, ships visited,
                    papers taken, crews given ten minutes to take to boats. Some other boats
                    captured and taken to port. Some chased and run aground.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
